{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/how-games-make-money/audio/main-7e4e16e3d7f6.mp3","durationSec":182.856,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.9,"text":"A game needs a team and technology."},{"start":2.68,"end":3.84,"text":"Programmers write code."},{"start":3.84,"end":5.96,"text":"Artists make characters and worlds."},{"start":6.54,"end":9.68,"text":"Other workers test the game, answer players, and fix problems."},{"start":10.52,"end":14.06,"text":"Online games also need computers called servers so people can play together."},{"start":14.8,"end":17.34,"text":"A company can ask players to buy a game before playing."},{"start":18.08,"end":21,"text":"Another game can be free to start and sell extra things later."},{"start":21.48,"end":22.98,"text":"This is called free-to-play."},{"start":22.98,"end":26.42,"text":"Free-to-play does not mean the game has no business plan."},{"start":26.86,"end":30.72,"text":"The company still needs income to pay its costs and continue its work."},{"start":31.54,"end":33.18,"text":"Many games have a store inside them."},{"start":33.18,"end":39.8,"text":"Official Fortnite information says players can use V-Bucks for Battle Passes, cosmetics, and other items."},{"start":40.42,"end":43.72,"text":"It also describes the Item Shop, outfits, and emotes."},{"start":43.72,"end":46.76,"text":"V-Bucks are a virtual currency used in Fortnite."},{"start":47.56,"end":52.3,"text":"Roblox has a Marketplace where users can find and buy items for a customizable avatar."},{"start":52.82,"end":56.78,"text":"Roblox creator information also explains purchases made with Robux."},{"start":57.36,"end":60.38,"text":"A skin or outfit can make a character feel more personal."},{"start":61.02,"end":64.42,"text":"However, a digital item is not a physical toy that you can hold."},{"start":64.42,"end":70.62,"text":"Virtual currency can make the real cost less easy to notice, so it helps to check the price carefully."},{"start":71.92,"end":73.88,"text":"Games can earn money in several other ways."},{"start":74.5,"end":79.84,"text":"Roblox creator information describes passes that give a player a special privilege after one payment."},{"start":80.44,"end":85.42,"text":"It also describes subscriptions with a payment each month and immersive ads inside an experience."},{"start":86.22,"end":92.12,"text":"Fortnite documentation describes the Battle Pass as a way to unlock cosmetics, V-Bucks, and other items."},{"start":93.16,"end":95.06,"text":"Rewarded ads are common in phone games."},{"start":95.52,"end":99.58,"text":"A player chooses to watch a short ad and receives coins or an extra life."},{"start":100.3,"end":104.56,"text":"The advertiser pays to show the ad, and part of that money goes to the game business."},{"start":105.08,"end":110.54,"text":"Together, these examples show how video games make money without charging every player in the same way."},{"start":111.26,"end":115.3,"text":"A game may run a limited-time event and offer a special character or item."},{"start":116.22,"end":118.18,"text":"The short time can make the item feel rare."},{"start":118.18,"end":120.72,"text":"Players may worry that they will miss their chance."},{"start":121.58,"end":125.04,"text":"This feeling is often called FOMO, or fear of missing out."},{"start":125.7,"end":129.58,"text":"A timer tells you when an offer ends, but it does not mean you need the item."},{"start":130.14,"end":132.54,"text":"The item might return later, or it might not."},{"start":133.44,"end":136.92,"text":"Game companies use events to bring players back and show them new offers."},{"start":137.62,"end":144.26,"text":"A useful choice is to pause, check the real price, and decide after the first excitement becomes quieter."},{"start":145.38,"end":150.68,"text":"New maps, characters, missions, and rewards give players a reason to return."},{"start":151.36,"end":156,"text":"When more people play for longer, they also have more chances to see a store or an ad."},{"start":156,"end":160.38,"text":"Updates can therefore support both the fun of a game and its business."},{"start":161.4,"end":164.52,"text":"Before spending, set a budget and ask a few questions."},{"start":165.56,"end":168.58,"text":"Do I really want this, or am I reacting to FOMO?"},{"start":169.26,"end":170.84,"text":"Will I use this pass often?"},{"start":171.52,"end":173.64,"text":"What else could I buy with the same real money?"},{"start":174.68,"end":177.96,"text":"A child can also ask a parent or another trusted adult."},{"start":178.98,"end":182.34,"text":"A skin may be worth it to one player and not worth it to another."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"game","start":0.18,"end":0.42},{"text":"needs","start":0.42,"end":0.72},{"text":"a","start":0.72,"end":0.86},{"text":"team","start":0.86,"end":1.14},{"text":"and","start":1.14,"end":1.3},{"text":"technology","start":1.3,"end":1.9},{"text":"Programmers","start":2.68,"end":3.16},{"text":"write","start":3.16,"end":3.42},{"text":"code","start":3.42,"end":3.84},{"text":"Artists","start":3.84,"end":4.52},{"text":"make","start":4.52,"end":4.78},{"text":"characters","start":4.78,"end":5.32},{"text":"and","start":5.32,"end":5.62},{"text":"worlds","start":5.62,"end":5.96},{"text":"Other","start":6.54,"end":6.7},{"text":"workers","start":6.7,"end":7.06},{"text":"test","start":7.06,"end":7.34},{"text":"the","start":7.34,"end":7.56},{"text":"game","start":7.56,"end":7.84},{"text":"answer","start":8.16,"end":8.38},{"text":"players","start":8.38,"end":8.78},{"text":"and","start":8.94,"end":9.02},{"text":"fix","start":9.02,"end":9.22},{"text":"problems","start":9.22,"end":9.68},{"text":"Online","start":10.52,"end":10.78},{"text":"games","start":10.78,"end":11.14},{"text":"also","start":11.14,"end":11.44},{"text":"need","start":11.44,"end":11.7},{"text":"computers","start":11.7,"end":12.14},{"text":"called","start":12.14,"end":12.46},{"text":"servers","start":12.46,"end":12.8},{"text